  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of sustainability has become increasingly important in recent years. It refers to the ability of a system or process to maintain itself over time without depleting its resources. In other words, it is about living within our means and not exploiting the planet's natural resources for short-term gains.\n\nA sustainable future requires a fundamental shift in the way we think about development. We need to move away from the idea that economic growth is the only measure of success. Instead, we should prioritize social and environmental well-being alongside economic progress.\n\nThis change will not be easy, but it is necessary if we want to create a better world for future generations. It requires a new mindset, one that values long-term thinking over short-term gains. We need to invest in renewable energy sources, reduce waste, and promote sustainable agriculture practices.\n\nThe benefits of sustainability are numerous. Not only does it help preserve the planet's natural resources, but it also creates jobs and stimulates economic growth in the long run. However, the transition to a more sustainable future will require significant investment and effort from governments, businesses, and individuals alike.\",\n\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the article?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The importance of economic growth\", \"The need for sustainability in modern society\", \"The benefits of renewable energy sources\", \"The role of governments in promoting sustainable development\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The need for sustainability in modern society\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what is a key characteristic of a sustainable system?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It can maintain itself over time without depleting its resources\", \"It prioritizes economic growth above all else\", \"It relies heavily on fossil fuels\", \"It ignores social and environmental well-being\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It can maintain itself over time without depleting its resources\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards the current state of development?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Positive, as it has led to significant economic growth\", \"Negative, as it prioritizes short-term gains over long-term sustainability\", \"Neutral, as it is a necessary evil\", \"Ambivalent, as it depends on individual perspectives\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Negative, as it prioritizes short-term gains over long-term sustainability\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is one of the benefits of adopting sustainable practices?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It leads to significant economic losses in the short term\", \"It creates jobs and stimulates economic growth in the long run\", \"It has no impact on the environment or society\", \"It requires minimal investment from governments and individuals\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It creates jobs and stimulates economic growth in the long run\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what is required for a sustainable future?\",\n      \"options\": [\"A significant reduction in government spending\", \"A fundamental shift in the way we think about development\", \"A complete reliance on fossil fuels\", \"A focus solely on economic growth\"],\n      \"answer\": \"A fundamental shift in the way we think about development\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
